Directory {

@@ ===========================================================================
@@
@@	DB48X speed test - see issue #1725
@@
@@	Five timings. Each program runs its own TEVAL and leaves the elapsed
@@	time on the stack, in milliseconds. Nothing else is measured and
@@	nothing is stored.
@@
@@	Iteration counts differ, so divide each time by its count before
@@	comparing. The number that matters is the cost of Tget divided by the
@@	cost of Tadd, per iteration:
@@
@@	    desktop simulator, x86-64    1.18
@@	    DM32 hardware                0.89
@@	    Samsung Galaxy S20 FE        8.0
@@
@@	Author & design          : Jean Wilson
@@	Co-authors & programming : Claude & Claude Code (Anthropic)
@@
@@ ===========================================================================


@@ ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
@@	Tadd - integer addition, 100000 times
@@	The interpreter baseline: no array is involved anywhere.
@@ ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

Tadd
«
	« 1 100000 FOR i 1 2 + DROP NEXT » TEVAL
»


@@ ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
@@	Tpush - push an array literal and drop it, 100000 times
@@	The array is never read, only placed on the stack and discarded.
@@ ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

Tpush
«
	« 1 100000 FOR i [ 5000 10000 2100 ] DROP NEXT » TEVAL
»


@@ ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
@@	Tget - read one element of an array, 10000 times
@@	This is the operation under investigation.
@@ ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

Tget
«
	« 1 10000 FOR i [ 5000 10000 2100 ] 1 GET DROP NEXT » TEVAL
»


@@ ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
@@	Tarr - add two arrays, 10000 times
@@	Reads three elements and builds a new array.
@@ ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

Tarr
«
	« 1 10000 FOR i [ 5000 10000 2100 ] DUP + DROP NEXT » TEVAL
»


@@ ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
@@	Tlam - full Lambert solver, 10000 times
@@	A real workload: reads two 3-vectors, runs a bounded secant loop,
@@	builds the result.
@@ ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

Tlam
«
	« 1 10000 FOR i [ 5000 10000 2100 ] [ -14600 2500 7000 ] 3600 398600 LambertUN DROP NEXT » TEVAL
»

}


@@ ===========================================================================
@@	Tell the tester what to do next
@@ ===========================================================================

"Test de vitesse charge.

Touche VAR : 5 programmes.
Executez-les un par un :
Tadd Tpush Tget Tarr Tlam

Notez chaque temps en ms."

VariablesMenu
